WEBVTT

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.990
AUGUST 11, 2095 - MIRAGE BAT FINAL

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:26.050
Mirage Bat is supposed to be the crown
jewel of the Nine Schools Competition...

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.010
but this feels anticlimactic.

00:00:28.010 --> 00:00:30.760
If First High wins this event...

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.890
it'll seal their overall victory.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.390
For the other schools...

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:37.930
it's already more or less a throwaway match.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:39.270
My bad.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.600
If only I'd won the Monolith Code Event!

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:44.310
No, I'm to blame for that, too.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.480
My dream of Third High
winning the tournament

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.820
and getting to dance with Miyuki Shiba
at the party on the last day...

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.120
is hanging by a thread now!

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.330
Huh?

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.450
But it's not as if all hope is lost!

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.540
I'm begging you, Isshiki!
Win this thing!

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:01.540
For the sake of my dream!

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.630
Masaki?

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.440
So, they're not here, after all?

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.860
I'm sorry. It doesn't look
like I can make it to the arena.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.530
That's all right.
Even if you don't come to my match,

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:41.000
I promise to acquit myself well
as a member of the Isshiki Family.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.160
Airi...

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.170
You don't have to take on such a load.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:51.300
Battle for what's truly dear to you.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.220
Mother...

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:58.970
The task that I must accomplish
is to go all out and win this match!

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.470
That's all!

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.020
The Mirage Bat Official Event Final...

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:05.900
is now underway!

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.050
Are all of the players using Flying Magic?

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.600
Just as I thought.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.180
I had a feeling this'd happen

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:06.730
the moment my brother submitted
my CAD to the tournament officials.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.440
How reckless is that?

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.520
It's not the kind of magic
you can master on the fly.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.190
I can't believe they're prioritizing victory
over their players' safety!

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:16.530
There's nothing to worry about.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:17.610
Huh?

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:24.370
Because they appear to be using the
sequence unveiled by Taurus Silver as is.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:28.580
If anything happens,
the safety mechanism should kick in.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.370
Right, we're totally flying!

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.630
Feels great!

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.460
Huh?

00:04:35.380 --> 00:04:36.920
N-No way!

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:42.390
But we're using the same magic!

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.350
I knew it! I can't beat Shiba
if all I can do is fly!

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.650
So, that's the safety mechanism?

00:04:56.650 --> 00:05:01.700
Yes. It automatically activates
when the remaining Psion level dips.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.620
Thank goodness!

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:12.000
It seems like this is good publicity
for the new magic, as well.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:12.920
Couldn't ask for more.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:19.590
Thank you for giving Flying Magic
such a gorgeous debut, Miyuki.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.090
Three of us left!

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.970
This ensures a Top 3 finish for First High!

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.480
First High is now also a lock
to win the tournament!

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:34.270
So, I'm just going to end up
trailing in her wake?

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:40.490
So far away. Because she practiced more?
Or because she's more talented?

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:45.070
No! That can't be it! It can't be!

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:47.120
But...

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.250
the overall victor has been determined.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.540
There's no longer any reason
to continue with this match.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.460
Mother...

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.430
Battle for what's truly dear to you.

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.550
Give it your all.

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.470
Airi!

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:15.560
Very well, Mother.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:17.810
I will...

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:27.740
I will not give up!

00:06:39.380 --> 00:06:43.260
A blend of Flying Magic and the
Jump Spell that I'm accustomed to...

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:45.630
This is me playing for keeps!

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.890
This is me going all out!

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.820
This isn't going to end well, is it?

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:03.820
Right.

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:09.410
Using a Jump Spell on top of the Flying Magic
that she isn't even used to wielding...

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.280
Isshiki's not going to last long.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:16.580
Still, Airi opted to use that magic
despite being fully aware of the risks.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:20.210
Not giving up...
All for the sake of victory!

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.710
Isshiki...

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.630
To think that you've learned
to wield Flying Magic at this level

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.380
in such a short time...

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.050
Miyuki!

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:31.720
--Come on!
--Go!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.390
Miyuki!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.020
Thank you, everyone!

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.770
"FINAL"
"MIYUKI SHIBA, AIRI ISSHIKI,
SAKIKO SASAKAWA, YUKIKO ISHIOKA"

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.230
Good job!

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:44.610
You were awesome!

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:46.530
Thank you very much.

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.320
There will now be a break.

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.870
What are you so afraid of, Airi?

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:01.080
I'm the one who adjusted your CAD.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.040
You can fly better than that.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:04.800
Higher, faster.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:08.300
So, trust in your own abilities!

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.140
And in me!

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:15.140
Thanks, Shiori.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.180
Even if Miyuki did nothing
the rest of the way,

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:21.190
First High's overall victory
would be in the bag, but...

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:23.190
She's not going to do that. No way.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.320
Nope!

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:27.570
She wouldn't be Miyuki if she did, right?

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.450
I'm going to battle until the end!

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.530
I know quite well
that I'm putting my own needs first!

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:38.040
And I do understand
the significance of this match!

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:43.000
But that's exactly why
I want to battle until the end!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.250
Please let me do so!

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:48.630
Miyuki, you can do as you please.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.130
Go fly to your heart's content.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.260
Right!

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:59.350
Considering that we've already won overall,
I probably should've stopped her.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.390
I'm such a pushover, aren't I?

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.940
No. I respect you...

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.570
President.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:20.160
Watch me, Mother, Shiori, Toko, Ms. Mizuo,
as I go into battle with those I care about.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.210
This is me at this moment!

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:27.800
Isshiki...

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:31.470
So, there's something
that's sacrosanct to you, too?

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:35.300
This match isn't mine alone.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.270
The only reason
I can take my place on this stage...

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:41.180
is because everyone else fought so hard.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:46.440
I want to live up to the expectations
of everyone who got me here!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:47.860
And...

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:51.700
I have feelings
that are sacrosanct, as well!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:04.040
Because this is my brother's magic!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.920
Because these are the wings
my brother gave me!

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:10.510
I want a victory
that's worthy of my brother!

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:11.630
Not yet!

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:24.770
--Miyuki!
--Miyuki! Come on!

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:27.230
Go! That's it!

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:30.360
Airi...

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:31.990
You can't...

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:39.870
Miyuki...

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.970
AUGUST 11, 2095 - NIGHT

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.480
Hello, members of No-Head Dragon...

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.070
East Japan Branch.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:21.490
SAME DAY - SAME TIME

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.830
There's just no beating a post-match bath, huh?

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:24.960
Although Miyuki was
the only one actually in the match.

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.130
Brother...

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:30.960
Please be safe.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:37.300
Ah! What a coincidence!

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.480
Congratulations on winning, Shiba.

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:55.740
Thank you, Isshiki.

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:18.010
H-Hold on, will you?
We'll back off from this plot!

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:20.140
We'll withdraw
from this country, as well!

00:12:20.140 --> 00:12:22.050
So--

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.810
B-But why?

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:27.310
We didn't kill anyone, remember?

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:33.860
I don't care how many people
you killed or how many you let live.

00:12:33.860 --> 00:12:38.240
You people messed with something
you never should've touched.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:43.370
That's reason enough
for you to meet your demise.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:45.450
You demon!

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.080
Demon, huh?

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:48.620
That's right.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:53.590
Because you drew out
my one remaining emotion...

00:12:53.590 --> 00:12:57.840
I was finally able
to unleash this demonic power.

00:12:57.840 --> 00:13:00.970
D-Demonic power?

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:03.010
This spell... Don't tell me...

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.810
it's that spell
from three years ago in Okinawa!

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:08.060
Demon Light?

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:32.000
I'm never going to let
anything like that happen again.

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:51.140
I find this moment a bit awkward.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:54.690
I'm not sure if my words and attitude
might seem arrogant or not,

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:57.480
so it makes me hesitant.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:01.190
I just had to thank you for something.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:02.450
What?

00:14:02.450 --> 00:14:05.620
It was brought home to me
during today's match.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:12.290
Your sheer talent as well as the overwhelming
gap between your abilities and my own...

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:13.670
But...

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:18.710
I realized something
after taking you on.

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:21.130
That is, my own potential.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.090
Potential?

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:26.970
Using my Jump Spell
simultaneously with Flying Magic...

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:30.390
Without you, it never would've
occurred to me to try that.

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:34.190
I'll be able to fly faster
if I practice more.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:39.070
I may have lost the match,
but I did gain an incredible experience.

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.900
That's why I wanted to thank you.

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:46.360
Thank you, Shiba.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.580
To be able to think that way...

00:14:49.580 --> 00:14:52.080
You're just as amazing as I thought!

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:54.710
You're the one who's amazing.

00:14:54.710 --> 00:15:00.800
I was lucky to get the chance
to battle someone my own age like you.

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:05.380
Likewise. You were so powerful,
you had me in quite a frenzy!

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:06.970
Really?

00:15:06.970 --> 00:15:09.220
Then I'm really honored.

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:14.230
Next year, I'll be even better,
and I'll put you into more of a frenzy.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.810
Well! I'm not going down in defeat!

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:22.070
Maybe I'll give that a try, too.

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:38.750
Brother!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.510
Welcome back!

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:46.630
I'm so glad that you're safe!

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:52.140
Thanks. I'm back...

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:53.270
Miyuki.

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:02.640
AUGUST 12, 2095 - LAST DAY OF THE NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION - AFTER-PARTY

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:13.700
H-Huh? Y-You're brother and sister?

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:15.950
You never realized that until now, then?

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:17.460
Masaki!

00:16:18.420 --> 00:16:23.340
So, my brother and I didn't
look like siblings to you, Ichijo.

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:25.550
I never dreamed you were Shiba's brother!

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:27.920
You don't look a thing like her,
so how could I realize?

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.180
Masaki! Anyone would realize that!

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:33.510
Shiba! May I have...
May I have this dance? Just this one dance?

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:35.850
We're leaving, Masaki!

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.850
What's wrong?

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:41.190
I really think that Tatsuya
was the driving force behind today's victory.

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:42.650
I agree.

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:46.690
He really came up big for us
both as an engineer and as a player!

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:50.530
So, if he's all that,
how can he be a Course 2 student?

00:16:50.530 --> 00:16:51.740
What?

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:56.700
He's far superior to me
both in terms of knowledge and technique.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:17:00.040
Even so, Tatsuya's a Course 2 student.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:03.340
What's the difference
between Course 1 and Course 2 students?

00:17:03.340 --> 00:17:08.470
Why do people throw around terms
like "irregular student" and "honor student"?

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:10.340
Tatsuya's special.

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:12.930
In terms of magic engineering
know-how and technology,

00:17:12.930 --> 00:17:15.310
no one can hold a candle to Tatsuya.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:17.100
The difference between Course 1 and Course 2

00:17:17.100 --> 00:17:19.020
is the difference in
practical skills test scores.

00:17:19.020 --> 00:17:20.310
That's all.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:23.100
Is this uniform to blame maybe?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:25.440
Originally, it was just a matter of...

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:27.940
not getting the embroidery done in time
when the student body expanded.

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.030
Huh?

00:17:29.030 --> 00:17:30.320
What?

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.530
A-chan, you didn't know?

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.950
To increase the number of magicians,

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:38.830
the school recruited more students
in the middle of the school year.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:41.120
That's how Course 2 students came to be.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.330
But there was a shortage of instructors,

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.750
so the additional students
ended up studying only theory,

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.880
with practical skills having to wait
until the new school year.

00:17:47.880 --> 00:17:53.130
But then, someone messed up
the order for new uniforms,

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:56.890
and the Course 2 students' uniforms
had no emblem.

00:17:56.890 --> 00:17:59.100
M-Messed up the order?

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:02.980
On top of that, they never did
remedy the instructor shortage.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:06.570
So the misunderstanding was confirmed,
or should I say "ignored"?

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:09.610
And that's why we have our
current Course 1-Course 2 system.

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:15.280
At this point, you'd think it'd be more of a
hassle to make two types of uniforms, right?

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:19.700
S-So all that intense hostility,
thanks to a stupid reason like that?

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:22.000
Well, it's also a fact that...

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:26.960
that stupid reason was spurred on
by some Course 1 students' sense of elitism.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:34.180
That's why I wanted to do something
about it while I was here.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:38.050
Oh, by the way, under no circumstances
can Miyuki ever know, okay?

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:40.270
R-Right! Of course!

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:43.560
If she ever found out,
it would be disastrous!

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:44.810
What's going on?

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:45.980
Huh?

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:47.900
Oh, it's nothing!

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:56.160
Um, by the way,
have any of you seen my brother?

00:18:56.160 --> 00:18:58.700
Oh, if you're looking for Tatsuya,

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:02.290
Jumonji just asked him to meet him
down on the courtyard.

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:05.330
What?

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:08.380
"May I have this dance, Shiba?"

00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:11.460
"It would be my pleasure, Mr. Jumonji!"

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.380
As if that would ever happen!

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:15.930
Surely not! Brother!

00:19:27.980 --> 00:19:29.900
It's Mr. Jumonji!

00:19:29.900 --> 00:19:31.860
Meaning that...

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:34.150
Brother!

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.780
What's wrong? You shouldn't run
like that at night. It's dangerous.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:43.250
Yes. But... Um, what were you
meeting Mr. Jumonji for?

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:45.540
It wasn't a big deal.

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:48.580
We were discussing
what would happen after they graduated.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:52.090
Have Tatsuya join the Ten Master Clans
through a political marriage?

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:55.720
See, the fact that he soundly defeated
the Ichijo heir apparent

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:58.130
created quite the stir at the Clan meeting.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:01.850
Oh, I see. Well, what can you do?

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:07.270
You can try to pass a jewel off as a pebble,
but only for so long.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:08.810
Right.

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:12.770
The time will come for everyone
to choose their own futures

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:16.030
according to their respective
positions and abilities.

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:22.200
But the more competent a person is,
the more that may end up shackling them.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:23.450
But...

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:25.000
I'm sure that those kids...

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:29.000
They've started playing the last song.

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:34.300
Brother...

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:38.800
Will you please dance
the last dance with me?

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:45.020
With pleasure.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.350
Did you enjoy the Nine Schools Competition?

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:52.650
Yes!

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:53.770
Once again...

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:59.450
it made me glad from the bottom of my heart
that we enrolled at this Magic High School.

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:03.410
Wonderful friends, upperclassmen
whom I can look up to,

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:06.370
and worthy rivals to compete against.

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:09.920
Magic has connected me to everyone.

00:21:09.920 --> 00:21:12.750
These encounters have taught me

00:21:12.750 --> 00:21:16.170
how wonderful it is
to strive for the top together.

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:20.720
If there's still something
I don't know about magic,

00:21:20.720 --> 00:21:24.430
then encounters themselves
might be magic, don't you agree?

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:25.760
I think you're right.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:33.940
Was our meeting magic, too, I wonder.

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:35.360
Or perhaps...

00:23:07.110 --> 00:23:10.950
JANUARY 9, 2096

00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:15.420
I wonder how Shizuku's doing in America.

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:17.160
I really miss her!

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:18.920
You're still going on like that?

00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:21.800
It's just a foreign exchange program
for three months, right?

00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:23.420
It's high time you got used to the idea.

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:26.090
All right! Then let's give her a call!

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:27.680
It's evening over there now!

00:23:27.680 --> 00:23:29.350
Good idea!

00:23:34.520 --> 00:23:36.140
Hello!

00:23:36.980 --> 00:23:39.690
Is this the classroom for First Year, Class A?

00:23:39.690 --> 00:23:43.740
Oh, are you the foreign student
who just arrived today?

00:23:46.320 --> 00:23:47.740
Nice to meet you.

00:23:47.740 --> 00:23:50.280
Welcome to First High School!
